---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../config';
---
<Base title="Privacy" description="What this site collects about its readers: nothing beyond standard server logs. No cookies, no analytics, no advertising." eyebrow="About" lede="This site does not track its readers." reviewed="2026-11-20" toc={false}>
  <h2 id="what-we-collect">What the site collects</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>No cookies.</strong> The site sets none.</li>
    <li><strong>No analytics or advertising scripts.</strong> No third-party code runs on any page.</li>
    <li><strong>No accounts, forms or newsletters.</strong> The site never asks for your name or email address.</li>
    <li><strong>Fonts and scripts are served from this site.</strong> Reading a page does not contact any other company’s servers.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="server-logs">Server logs</h2>
  <p>
    Like every website, the hosting provider records basic request information such as the time, the page requested
    and the requesting address, in order to operate the service and protect it from abuse. The publisher does not use
    these logs to identify readers.
  </p>

  <h2 id="search">Search</h2>
  <p>
    The search page works entirely in your browser. What you type is matched against an index file downloaded from
    this site and is not sent anywhere.
  </p>

  <h2 id="email">If you write to us</h2>
  <p>
    If you email <a href={`mailto:${site.correctionsEmail}`}>{site.correctionsEmail}</a>, your message and address are
    used only to handle your request. A correction is described in the <a href="/updates/">update log</a> without
    naming the person who asked for it, unless they ask to be named.
  </p>

  <h2 id="external-links">Links to other sites</h2>
  <p>
    Source links lead to third-party sites with their own privacy practices. Following a link tells that site you
    arrived from here unless your browser withholds it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="people-named">Information about people named on the site</h2>
  <p>
    The site reports only material already published in official records and established reporting. It does not
    publish home addresses, contact details, family information or other private data, and it does not name people
    who made complaints. See the <a href="/about/#corrections">corrections policy</a> to raise a concern.
  </p>
</Base>
